Track 2: Squelch-Talk Parley
- Story & Context: Silas crouched beneath the traffic junction box, his fingertips raw from overriding the encryption keys, while the rhythmic chirping of the signal lamps turned into an aggressive, polyrhythmic trance beat that forced the patrolling officers to retreat to their cruisers. "Is the hum of the wire the ghost of our own greed?" he questioned the static, recording the sound of their confusion to weave into the bassline for his confession piece.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: An extreme close-up of copper wires pulsing with raw electricity, sparks forming abstract shapes like jagged nerves, dark oil stains on textured road concrete in the background.

Track 3: The Kelvin-Helmholtz Collapse
- Story & Context: By the time the authorities finally cut the power to the main plaza, the resonance from the final trumpet blow had already caused a visible rift in the cloud cover above the park, a permanent atmospheric scar left behind as the Signal Saboteurs vanished into the fog. The air felt heavy with the scent of wet soot, a myth solidified in the silence that followed the, "Breathe out the fire and let the copper melt," which became the movement's unofficial epitaph inscribed on every destroyed street sign.
